@startuml wt_common_switch
title Common WT switch exchange
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 75
actor "User i" as U
participant "ST i" as ST
participant "Niso i" as N
participant "Boomlet i" as B
participant "Other four Boomlets" as P
participant "Candidate WT" as C
participant "Bound SAR i" as S

legend left
Logical authenticated paths may be relayed by Nisos.
Each of the other four peers performs its own review and local service checks.
endlegend

group Review and freeze
  N -> B: Propose a different setup-roster candidate
  B -> B: Build manifest and resume-package commitment
  B -> ST: Authenticated nonce-bound review commitment
  ST -> U: Display setup, scope, both WTs and recovery policy
  U -> ST: Approve
  ST -> B: Signed nonce-bound review
  B -> B: Verify review against unchanged local state
  B -> B: Persist exact intent and freeze ordinary advancement
  B -> P: Signed intent, manifest and committed package evidence
  P -> B: Four signed intents and committed evidence
  B -> B: Verify all five, own exact intent and compatible scope
  B -> B: Derive common wt_switch_id and recovery mode
end

group Candidate preparation
  N -> C: Five intents, setup agreement and reconstruction evidence
  C -> C: Verify roster membership, signatures, packages and phase gates
  C -> N: Registration and payment requirements
  N -> C: Required registration and payment evidence
  C -> B: Candidate setup receipt through Niso
  B -> C: Bound SAR identity and authenticated switch probe
  C -> S: Forward probe to the exact SAR
  S -> C: Signed probe response encrypted to Boomlet i
  C -> B: Forward exact response
  B -> B: Verify own receipt, payment and fresh SAR response
  note over P,C
    The other four peers independently finish their local prerequisites.
    Candidate retains the five committed reconstruction packages.
  end note
  C -> B: Signed deterministic ready commitment
  C -> P: Same signed readiness content
  B -> B: Verify candidate readiness and derive activation digest
end

group Ballot zero
  B -> B: Persist PREPARE(ACTIVATE)
  B -> P: PREPARE
  P -> B: Four matching PREPARE votes
  B -> B: Verify and durably retain five-vote PreparedCertificate
  B -> B: Persist COMMIT for the same ballot and value
  B -> P: COMMIT
  P -> P: Each verifies five PREPARE votes, retains their certificate,\nand persists matching COMMIT before export
  P -> B: Four matching COMMIT votes
  B -> B: Verify final five-vote DecisionCertificate
  B -> P: Relay complete DecisionCertificate
  B -> C: Complete ACTIVATE DecisionCertificate
  B -> B: Atomically install new head and candidate index
  P -> P: Each peer installs after verifying the final certificate
  C -> C: Begin coordination under the certified head
end

note over B,C
  Continue the retained phase only after local certificate installation.
  A timeout or cancellation enters 07_decision_recovery.puml.
  Ordinary withdrawal state remains frozen until a final decision.
end note
@enduml
